// A `for ... by` over 100,000 entities: built --parallel their keys are
// listed and sorted on many threads (from 16,384 on), by the same passes,
// so in the same order as on one: those alike in the order they are
// stored, those below nought first. Its body only gives rows to buffers,
// so the entities are visited on many threads too, each writing its rows
// at its place in the order (one to `Seen`, two to `Twice`, between
// them). The rows, as hashes, the same both ways, each time.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/ordered_parallel.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.one
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/ordered_parallel.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.all
// RUN: cmp %t.one %t.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.one

// CHECK:      step 0: 100000 rows, order 5796329773731977640, 200000 rows two each, 18044514214991199808
// CHECK-NEXT: step 1: 100000 rows, order 3085602959123592563, 200000 rows two each, 13725720965719220983
// CHECK:      step 4: 100000 rows, order 6974316037733467605, 200000 rows two each, 8109710512045392201
